<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n3876" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄλαστος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, (cf.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄληστος</span>): (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ-</span> priv., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λαθεῖν,
		λήθομαι</span>): —<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>not to be forgotten. insufferable</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πένθος, ἄχος</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				24.105
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				4.108
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hes.
				<u>Th.</u>
				467
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Alcm.
				23
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Pers.</u>
				990
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔπαθον ἄλαστα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>OC</u>
					538
				</span></i>
			: 
				Sup.
			
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ότατον, πῆμα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>IG</u>
					12
				</span></i>
			 (<i><span class="en">
				5
			</span></i>). <i><span class="en">
				64
			</span></i> (<span class="entity">Naxos</span>); neut. as Adv.,
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄλαστον ὀδύρομαι</span> I wail
				<i>inconsolably</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				14.174
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				B.
				3.34
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> of persons, as
			in <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				22.261
			</span></i>, where Achilles calls Hector <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄλαστε</span>
			<i>thou whom I will never forget nor forgive!; accursed
			wretch</i>, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>OC</u>
				1482
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πατρὸς . . ἄ. αἷμα</span> ib.
				<i><span class="en">
				1672
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>Mim. Oxy.</u>
				413.60
			</span></i>.—Poet. and late Prose, Dempoh.<i><span class="en">
				<u>Sent.</u>
				13
			</span></i>: used by Trag. only in lyr.</div>
